visio flag marker, BEFORE - firmware at /tmp/before

1. A failed marker waits for the next boot
----------------------------------------------------------------------
    firmware: flag marker upload failed; /tmp/tmpetohwvuw/queue/FLAG_20260704_120030.marker stays queued for next-boot flush
  upload attempts in 2 s of outage: 1
  still queued: ['FLAG_20260704_120030.marker']
  -> one attempt, ever. The flag is stuck on the card until a reboot,
     and the nightly run scores that segment unflagged.

2. The startup flush sends segments before their flags
----------------------------------------------------------------------
    firmware: upload of /tmp/tmpo93jnmml/queue/20260704120300.mp4 failed; keeping it queued
    firmware: upload of /tmp/tmpo93jnmml/queue/FLAG_20260704_120030.marker failed; keeping it queued
    firmware: upload of /tmp/tmpo93jnmml/queue/FLAG_20260704_120401.marker failed; keeping it queued
  reached storage before the power went:
    device-sim/20260704120000.mp4
    device-sim/20260704120100.mp4
    device-sim/20260704120200.mp4
  still on the card: ['20260704120300.mp4', 'FLAG_20260704_120030.marker', 'FLAG_20260704_120401.marker']
  -> three segments up, neither flag. Name order puts digits before
     'FLAG_', so the footage always overtakes the flags.

3. A press has no local feedback at all
----------------------------------------------------------------------
  make_flag_press_handler parameters: ['queue_dir', 'submit', 'clock', 'cooldown']
  write_flag_marker syncs anything: False
  -> nothing to acknowledge with, and the marker is only as durable
     as the page cache: touch() and return.
